        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The detected clipboard command must also be on PATH (shutil.which): an environment that looks like X11 or Wayland with no copy tool installed marks nothing detected rather than suggesting a command that would fail.",
            "Under WSL every Windows profile's Downloads that exists is offered (at most three, the one matching $USER first), since the Windows user name can differ from the Linux one."
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Kept the key spelled [probe] clipboard_command and made it both-layer, rather than introducing a new key with an alias: the crafter keeps reading project files with no migration, and an Enter-through re-run still writes the same line.",
            "probe.clipboard_command sits last in WIZARD_WALK_ORDER_BOTH_LAYERS (11/19 in project mode); the renderer keeps [probe] where it was in the file.",
            "On a key with alternatives, a value made only of digits is read as a pick, and one out of range re-asks (the checkpoint picker rule); keys without alternatives keep reading digits as values (bools still take 0/1).",
            "In a list key each colon-separated entry may be a number (1:2, 1:inbox).",
            "The triple-quote refusal lives in effective_clipboard_command (and a warning on the wizard screen), not in load_config, so `bale config init` can still open and rewrite such a file; it applies at both layers so the key has one spelling everywhere.",
            ".baleignore signals: bulky or binary extensions, data or vendored directory names, and single files of 1 MiB or more, counted over the files pack would list, minus pack's baked-in excluded directories, heaviest first, at most six.",
            "A detector that cannot run (git missing, timeout) shows a one-line dim note on its key's screen instead of degrading silently."
          ],
